## Weekly Paid Media Report — Spend Movement

**Reporting windows:** last week = Oct 24–30, 2026 · prior week = Oct 17–23, 2026 · **Data complete through Oct 30, 2026** (all figures from the ad platforms — Google Ads, Meta Ads, Reddit Ads; data complete, no partial days).

### Account summary (total spend, all 3 platforms)

| Window | Total spend | Change |
|---|---|---|
| Prior week (Oct 17–23) | $9,892.11 | — |
| Last week (Oct 24–30) | $11,844.59 | **+$1,952.48 (+19.7%)** |

*(Total is the sum of the three platform figures below; no single tool returns a cross-platform total.)*

### Per-platform spend movement

| Platform | Prior week | Last week | Change |
|---|---|---|---|
| Google Ads | $5,377.43 | $8,029.35 | **+$2,651.92 (+49.3%)** |
| Meta Ads | $3,761.84 | $3,039.99 | **−$721.85 (−19.2%)** |
| Reddit Ads | $752.84 | $775.25 | **+$22.41 (+3.0%)** |

### What drove the total

The net +19.7% is almost entirely a **Google Ads ramp**: its +$2,651.92 increase outweighed Meta's −$721.85 pullback, with Reddit roughly flat. Spend share shifted from Meta (38.0% of prior-week spend → 25.7% last week) toward Google (54.4% → 67.8%).

Context from the same platform data: Google's spend increase was not an efficiency loss — conversions scaled with it (28 → 42, +50%) and CPA held essentially flat ($192.05 → $191.18). Meta spent less and converted slightly less (19 → 16), with CPA improving modestly ($197.99 → $190.00). The tooling doesn't expose *why* budget moved (e.g., campaign vs. auction-price changes), so the Google scale-up is a question to confirm with whoever manages bids/budgets, not a fact to assume.

### Caveats

- Reddit conversion volume is small (6–7/week); its metrics are noisy week to week.
- Only **spend** was explicitly compared via the window-comparison tool; conversions/CPA above are quoted from the two weekly totals per platform, not from a dedicated conversion comparison.
- Pipeline/revenue outcomes are not included — those live in the warehouse and are out of scope for this spend question.

If you'd like, I can propose a campaign change for any platform (e.g., whether to keep the Google ramp or rebalance toward Meta) — any such change would go through a pending proposal for your approval first.
